">n</span></span></span></span> denotes the length of the array. However, t=
his isn=E2=80=99t taking advantage of an important problem constraint: ther=
e are only three types of elements in the array.</p>
<p>To sort these numbers, we essentially want to position all 0s to the lef=
t, all 2s to the right, and any 1s in between. A key observation is that if=
 we place the 0s and the 2s in their correct positions, the 1s will automat=
ically be positioned correctly:</p>
