<p>This allows us to focus on only positioning two numbers.</p>
<p>One strategy we could use is to iterate through the array and move any 0=
s we encounter to the left, and any 2s we encounter to the right.</p>
<p>We can set a left pointer to move any 0s we encounter to the left, and a=
 right pointer to move any 2s to the right. To iterate through the array, w=
e can use a separate pointer, <code>i</code>:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>When we encounter a 0 at index <code>i</code>, swap it with <code>nums[l=
eft]</code>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When we encounter a 2 at index <code>i</code>, swap it with <code>nums[r=
ight]</code>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
